# Heartfire Hero's death trigger deals damage equal to its power. Bot2's Last Gasp on turn 2 gives the 1/1 -3/-3, so it dies with
# power -2 as it last existed (CR 608.2h). A negative power means no damage is dealt (CR 120.8), so the trigger resolves
# and neither Bot2 nor Bot1 changes life (both stay at 20); it must not deal 1 or 0-clamped-up damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Heartfire Hero
Island x5
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Last Gasp
Island x5
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Heartfire Hero.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Last Gasp.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Heartfire Hero)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Heartfire Hero
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Life = 20
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Heartfire Hero
